  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116612",
      "title": "Authoring SSR-ready Code (Beware of Pitfalls!)",
      "lectureOrder": 323,
      "videoOrder": 305,
      "sourceHash": "631a2d46e2251cb88d921f52ee5330e9313880f91acc9e73d62f41a5ba2438ae",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 3.42,
          "en": "Now, why are we getting this error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.42,
          "end": 6.24,
          "en": "when using server-side rendering?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.24,
          "end": 9.84,
          "en": "Well in the end it's coming from the TasksService file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.84,
          "end": 11.94,
          "en": "Because there in the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.94,
          "end": 15.87,
          "en": "I am reaching out to localStorage to load tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.87,
          "end": 19.323,
          "en": "because I'm using localStorage to store tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.43,
          "end": 23.4,
          "en": "But the problem now is that localStorage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 26.4,
          "en": "is a browser-side feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.4,
          "end": 30.51,
          "en": "so it's not available on the server-side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.51,
          "end": 33.72,
          "en": "and therefore when Angular tries to run this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.72,
          "end": 34.553,
          "en": "on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.553,
          "end": 38.28,
          "en": "which it does when it tries to pre-render the page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.28,
          "end": 41.013,
          "en": "we'll encounter this error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.12,
          "end": 45.483,
          "en": "So what can you do to make it work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.56,
          "end": 50.58,
          "en": "Well, one easy and recommended workaround",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.58,
          "end": 54.783,
          "en": "is to use the afterNextRender function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.28,
          "end": 58.38,
          "en": "This is a function about which you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.38,
          "end": 62.823,
          "en": "earlier in the course, you can import it from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.9,
          "end": 67.893,
          "en": "And this is a function that takes a function as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.85,
          "end": 72.93,
          "en": "and this function will then only be executed by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.93,
          "end": 75.663,
          "en": "after the next Component render cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 79.77,
          "en": "Now of course here we're still inside of a service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 79.77,
          "end": 81.81,
          "en": "but this service in the end is of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.81,
          "end": 84.06,
          "en": "being used from some Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.06,
          "end": 86.7,
          "en": "in the end, in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.7,
          "end": 87.72,
          "en": "And therefore, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 87.72,
          "end": 90.88,
          "en": "Components are being rendered by this application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 91.86,
          "end": 96.57,
          "en": "and afterNextRender does not care about which Component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.57,
          "end": 98.43,
          "en": "is being rendered next,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 98.43,
          "end": 102.24000000000001,
          "en": "it simply allows you to register a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 102.24000000000001,
          "end": 106.8,
          "en": "that executes some code that will be executed the next time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 106.8,
          "end": 109.47,
          "en": "after all Components have been rendered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 109.47,
          "end": 112.32,
          "en": "So the next time Angular is done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 112.32,
          "end": 116.22,
          "en": "going through all your Components and rendering them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 116.22,
          "end": 118.71000000000001,
          "en": "you could say, so the next time it's done rendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 118.71000000000001,
          "end": 121.95,
          "en": "that Component tree to the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 121.95,
          "end": 125.25,
          "en": "And therefore this also is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 125.25,
          "end": 128.7,
          "en": "that will only execute on the client-side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.7,
          "end": 132.84,
          "en": "because of course Angular does also render the Components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.84,
          "end": 135.9,
          "en": "and prepare some HTML code on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 135.9,
          "end": 139.47,
          "en": "but they're only rendered to the DOM on the client-side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 139.47,
          "end": 143.61,
          "en": "because the DOM only exists on the client-side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 143.61,
          "end": 146.88,
          "en": "and it's after that client-side render cycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.88,
          "end": 150.81,
          "en": "that this function which you pass to afterNextRender",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.81,
          "end": 152.73,
          "en": "will be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 152.73,
          "end": 155.16,
          "en": "And that's why inside of this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 155.16,
          "end": 159.3,
          "en": "you have a safe place for executing any code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.3,
          "end": 162.51,
          "en": "that must only run in the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.51,
          "end": 167.51,
          "en": "so that needs access to browser-side features, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.85,
          "end": 170.46,
          "en": "And now we can simply tell Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.46,
          "end": 174.84,
          "en": "that it's after the next overall Component render cycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.84,
          "end": 176.763,
          "en": "we want to execute this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.11,
          "end": 182.01,
          "en": "So this is a safe place to execute code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.01,
          "end": 185.94,
          "en": "that depends on the availability of the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 185.94,
          "end": 188.673,
          "en": "so that should not run on the server-side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 190.23,
          "end": 194.49,
          "en": "And therefore with this change made, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 194.49,
          "end": 198.573,
          "en": "and you stop that running server by pressing Ctrl + C,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 199.41,
          "end": 201.6,
          "en": "and you then run npm run build again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.6,
          "end": 204.87,
          "en": "to build the updated Angular project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.87,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "for server-side rendering.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 210.66,
          "en": "If you do that and you then run that command again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 210.66,
          "end": 214.07999999999998,
          "en": "to serve that server-side rendered application locally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 214.07999999999998,
          "end": 215.49,
          "en": "in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 215.49,
          "end": 220.35,
          "en": "If you now reload this page or visit some other user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 220.35,
          "end": 224.43,
          "en": "you'll see that now you are no longer getting an error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 224.43,
          "end": 227.07,
          "en": "because now this localStorage code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 227.07,
          "end": 231.603,
          "en": "really only runs in the browser, not anywhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
